IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `hda-types`

-- Housing and Development Act 1959 — GOALS 1-3: BUYING, DEALING WITH AND
-- LOSING A FLAT (Parts 4 and 4B: ss 50-74, 92).
--
--   Goal 1: "May this person buy a flat from the Board, and may the Board
--   cancel the application?" (ss 50, 57, 92)
--   Goal 2: "Is this dealing with a sold flat lawful, void, or one that needs
--   the Board's consent; is the flat protected from creditors?" (ss 52, 55,
--   56, 58, 59)
--   Goal 3: "May the Board re-enter, acquire or vest the flat, or penalise
--   the owner instead; and by when must each step be taken?" (ss 50(3)-(9),
--   59, 62-69, 74)
--
-- The Board's and the Minister's discretions are inputs.
-- Source: ../source/HDA1959.txt, Part 4.

§ `Goals 1-3 — the flat`

§§ `Goal 1 — buying a flat (ss 50, 57, 92)`

-- s 50(1): "A person is not entitled to purchase ... if the person, his or her
-- spouse or any authorised occupier — (a) is the owner of any other flat,
-- house, building or land or has an estate or interest therein; or (b) has, at
-- any time within 30 months immediately prior to the date of making an
-- application ..., or between the date of the application and the date of
-- completion ..., sold any flat, house, building or land ... or divested
-- himself or herself of any interest therein." (10): the Board may exempt;
-- s 57: a declared body corporate. FORK F1: a disposal exactly 30 months
-- before the application is within the period.
@ref ss 50(1), (10), 57
GIVEN p IS A `Purchase facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `entitled to purchase a flat from the Board` p IF
        p's `exempted by the Board or on the Minister's direction`
    OR  p's `a body corporate declared under s 57`
    OR  (    NOT p's `owns any other flat, house, building or land, or an interest in one`
         AND NOT `a disposal in the barred period`)
    WHERE
        `a disposal in the barred period` MEANS
            any (GIVEN d YIELD `barred` d) (p's `disposed of such property on`)
        `barred` d MEANS
                    ((d LESS THAN p's `application made on`) AND ((`add months` d 30) AT LEAST p's `application made on`))
                OR  ((d AT LEAST p's `application made on`) AND
                        CONSIDER p's `purchase completed on`
                        WHEN JUST c  THEN d AT MOST c
                        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE)

-- s 50(12): the Board "may cancel an application" on any of grounds (a)-(d).
@ref s 50(12)
GIVEN g IS A `Cancellation ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may cancel the application on` g IF NOT g EQUALS `none`

-- s 92(1): a buyer from an approved developer is ineligible "if the person or
-- his or her spouse is not entitled to purchase from the Board any flat ...
-- under Part 4".
@ref s 92(1)
GIVEN `person entitled under Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `spouse entitled under Part 4` IS A BOOLEAN, `the Minister allows otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `eligible to buy a DBSS flat, person entitled:` `person entitled under Part 4` `, spouse entitled:` `spouse entitled under Part 4` `, Minister allows:` `the Minister allows otherwise` IF
    `the Minister allows otherwise` OR (`person entitled under Part 4` AND `spouse entitled under Part 4`)

§§ `Goal 2 — dealings (ss 52, 55, 56, 58, 59)`

DECLARE `Effect of a dealing` IS ONE OF
    `lawful`
    `void`
    `may be declared void by the Board, and is a breach`
    `cannot be registered without the Board's consent`
    `a breach of the lease`

-- s 55(1)-(3): within the minimum occupation period, "except with the prior
-- written consent of the Board" an owner "must not ... sell or agree to sell";
-- a contract not in the prescribed form; such contracts "made on or after
-- 20 November 1998 in contravention ... [are] void".
-- s 56(1)-(2): no sale, lease, mortgage or disposal "without the prior written
-- consent of the Board"; if registered, the Board may declare it void.
-- s 58(1), (4): using protected property as security is void unless in favour
-- of the Board, an approved financial institution or a prescribed person;
-- (9)-(10): a trust without approval is void; (11): no resulting or
-- constructive trust. s 59(1): no registration of a transmission or transfer
-- on death without consent. s 52(3): a use the lease does not permit, without
-- approval.
@ref ss 52(3), 55(1)-(3), 56(1)-(2), 58(1), (4), (9)-(11), 59(1)
GIVEN d IS A `Dealing facts`
GIVETH AN `Effect of a dealing`
`the effect of` d MEANS
    IF (d's `the Board's prior written consent or approval`) AND (NOT `never cured by consent`)
    THEN `lawful`
    ELSE CONSIDER d's `dealing`
         WHEN `selling or agreeing to sell within the minimum occupation period` THEN
             IF d's `made on or after 20 November 1998` THEN `void` ELSE `a breach of the lease`
         WHEN `a sale contract not in the prescribed form` THEN
             IF d's `made on or after 20 November 1998` THEN `void` ELSE `a breach of the lease`
         WHEN `selling, leasing, mortgaging or otherwise disposing of the flat` THEN `may be declared void by the Board, and is a breach`
         WHEN `using the flat or its proceeds as security for a debt` permitted THEN
             IF permitted THEN `lawful` ELSE `void`
         WHEN `creating a trust of the flat`                        THEN `void`
         WHEN `claiming under a resulting or constructive trust`    THEN `void`
         WHEN `registering a transmission or transfer on the owner's death` THEN `cannot be registered without the Board's consent`
         WHEN `using the flat for a purpose the lease does not permit` THEN `a breach of the lease`
    WHERE
        `never cured by consent` MEANS
            d's `dealing` EQUALS `claiming under a resulting or constructive trust`

-- s 58(6): protected property does not vest in the Official Assignee on the
-- owner's bankruptcy; s 58(8): unless every owner is a non-citizen.
@ref s 58(6), (8)
GIVEN `all owners non-citizens` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `does not vest in the Official Assignee on bankruptcy, all owners non-citizens:` `all owners non-citizens` IF
    NOT `all owners non-citizens`

-- s 58(7): protected property is not attached in execution "unless the order
-- of the court is obtained by (a) a mortgagee ... under a mortgage created with
-- the prior written consent of the Board ...; or (b) a chargee ... under any
-- written law"; s 58(8): unless every owner is a non-citizen.
@ref s 58(7)-(8)
GIVEN `all owners non-citizens` IS A BOOLEAN, `a consented mortgagee or statutory chargee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may not be attached in execution, all owners non-citizens:` `all owners non-citizens` `, order obtained by a consented mortgagee or chargee:` `a consented mortgagee or statutory chargee` IF
    (NOT `all owners non-citizens`) AND (NOT `a consented mortgagee or statutory chargee`)

-- Both protections together: s 58(6)-(8) in the Official Assignee on
-- bankruptcy and is not attached in execution, unless by a consented
-- mortgagee or a statutory chargee — and neither protection applies if every
-- owner is a non-citizen.
@ref s 58(6)-(8)
GIVEN `all owners non-citizens` IS A BOOLEAN, `a consented mortgagee or statutory chargee` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `protected from bankruptcy and attachment, all owners non-citizens:` `all owners non-citizens` `, a consented mortgagee or chargee enforcing:` `a consented mortgagee or statutory chargee` IF
    (NOT `all owners non-citizens`) AND (NOT `a consented mortgagee or statutory chargee`)

-- s 59(3): the Board may vest the flat in itself where "(a) no representation
-- has been taken out ... within 12 months from the death ...; (b) ... the
-- personal representatives do not apply for the written consent ... within
-- 6 months from the date of representation; or (c) ... the sale or transfer
-- ... is not completed within 12 months from the date of that written
-- consent".
@ref s 59(3)
GIVEN died IS A DATE, represented IS A MAYBE DATE, applied IS A MAYBE DATE, consented IS A MAYBE DATE, completed IS A MAYBE DATE, `as at` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may vest a deceased owner's flat, died` died `, representation` represented `, applied for consent` applied `, consent` consented `, completed` completed `, as at` `as at` IF
    CONSIDER represented
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `as at` AT LEAST `add months` died 12
    WHEN JUST r  THEN
            r GREATER THAN `add months` died 12
        OR  `late` applied (`add months` r 6)
        OR  CONSIDER consented
            WHEN JUST c  THEN `late` completed (`add months` c 12)
            WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHERE
        `late` x deadline MEANS
            CONSIDER x
            WHEN JUST t  THEN t GREATER THAN deadline
            WHEN NOTHING THEN `as at` GREATER THAN deadline

§§ `Goal 3 — the Board's remedies (ss 62, 63, 74)`

-- s 62(1): the Board may re-enter and the lease determines "(a) if the rent ...
-- is unpaid for 3 calendar months after becoming payable and the Board has sent
-- a written demand by registered post ...; (b) if the owner has committed any
-- breach of a condition against assigning, underletting or parting with
-- possession ... or ... any other condition the breach of which is not capable
-- of remedy and the Board has sent a written notice ...; (c) if any condition
-- (being a condition the breach of which is capable of remedy) ... is not
-- performed or observed within 2 weeks after a written notice ...; (d) ... a
-- false statement in the owner's application form ...; (e) ... a breach of any
-- of the rules made under section 74(1)(g); or (f) ... used ... otherwise than
-- for the purpose permitted by the lease".
@ref s 62(1)
GIVEN r IS A `Re-entry facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may re-enter and determine the lease` r IF
        (r's `months rent unpaid after it became payable` AT LEAST 3 AND r's `a written demand sent by registered post`)
    OR  r's `breach of a non-assignment condition, or an irremediable breach, notified`
    OR  r's `days since notice of a remediable breach, still unremedied` GREATER THAN 14
    OR  r's `a false statement in the application form`
    OR  r's `a breach of rules under s 74(1)(g), in the Board's opinion`
    OR  r's `used otherwise than as the lease permits, without approval`

-- s 63(1)(a)-(o), with s 63(2): ground (b) does not apply to commercial
-- property bought with consent "not exceeding in value $250,000 or such higher
-- value as the Minister may allow" and used for business; (k) "3 calendar
-- months"; (m) an occupier "above the age of 14 years"; (o) at least one other
-- abatement or exclusion offence.
@ref s 63(1)-(2)
GIVEN g IS AN `Acquisition ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a ground for compulsory acquisition` g IF
    CONSIDER g
    WHEN `(b) owner, spouse or occupier acquired other property` value higher business THEN
        CONSIDER value
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST v  THEN NOT (business AND v AT MOST `the cap` higher)
    WHEN `(k) rent or payment unpaid 3 months after due, with notice of demand` months THEN months AT LEAST 3
    WHEN `(m) a conviction for throwing things from Board property` age occupier since1984 THEN
        since1984 AND ((NOT occupier) OR age GREATER THAN 14)
    WHEN `(o) repeated abatement or exclusion offences` others who appointed THEN
        who AND appointed AND others AT LEAST 1
    OTHERWISE TRUE
    WHERE
        `the cap` h MEANS
            CONSIDER h
            WHEN JUST x  THEN IF x GREATER THAN 250000 THEN x ELSE 250000
            WHEN NOTHING THEN 250000

GIVEN gs IS A LIST OF `Acquisition ground`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Board may compulsorily acquire the flat on` gs IF
    any (GIVEN g YIELD `a ground for compulsory acquisition` g) gs

-- s 74(1)(i)-(k): instead of proceeding under ss 50, 62 or 63, the Board may
-- (by rules) impose "a financial penalty not exceeding $50,000" for a breach on
-- or after 20 July 2015.
@ref s 74(1)(i)-(k)
GIVEN `breach on` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most financial penalty instead of ss 50, 62 or 63, breach on` `breach on` MEANS
    IF `breach on` AT LEAST YMD 2015 7 20 THEN 50000 ELSE 0

§§ `Goal 3 — the periods (ss 50, 59, 63, 66, 68, 69)`

DECLARE `Board step` IS ONE OF
    `s 50 vesting or termination after notice`       -- 14 days; appeal 14 days
    `s 59 vesting or rescission after notice`        -- 28 days; appeal 28 days
    `s 63 acquisition: objection after notice`       -- 28 days
    `s 63 acquisition: appeal after the Board's decision` -- 28 days
    `s 66 vesting where no objection was made`       -- 28 days after the s 63(3) notice
    `s 68 taking possession after notice`            -- 30 days
    `s 69 collecting movable property after notice`  -- at least 30 days

-- s 50(3A), (4): the Board waits 14 days after its notice; the purchaser may
-- appeal within 14 days. s 59(5A), (6): 28 days, and appeal within 28 days.
-- s 63(5), (7): objection within 28 days of the notice; appeal within 28 days
-- of the decision. s 66(1)(a)(i): vesting "on the expiry of a period of 28 days
-- after the date of service". s 68(1): possession "on the expiry of a period of
-- 30 days after the service of a notice". s 69(2): "at least 30 days".
@ref ss 50(3A)-(4), 59(5A)-(6), 63(5), (7), 66(1)(a)(i), 68(1), 69(2)
GIVEN s IS A `Board step`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days allowed for` s MEANS
    CONSIDER s
    WHEN `s 50 vesting or termination after notice` THEN 14
    WHEN `s 68 taking possession after notice`      THEN 30
    WHEN `s 69 collecting movable property after notice` THEN 30
    OTHERWISE 28

-- The Board may act once that many days after service have expired; an
-- objection or appeal is in time if made within that many days.
@ref ss 50(3A), 59(5A), 66(1), 68(1)
GIVEN s IS A `Board step`, served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest the Board may act on` s `, notice served` served MEANS
    served PLUS `the days allowed for` s PLUS 1

@ref ss 50(4), 59(6), 63(5), (7)
GIVEN s IS A `Board step`, served IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to object or appeal for` s `, served` served MEANS
    served PLUS `the days allowed for` s

-- s 15(1): the Board may vary a mortgage interest rate "upon giving the
-- mortgagor one month's notice".
@ref s 15(1)-(2)
GIVEN notice IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earliest a varied mortgage rate may apply, notice` notice MEANS `add months` notice 1

-- ss 28(14), 29(9): costs of urgent repairs are payable "within one month after
-- the date of the written notice or within such other period as the Board may
-- specify".
@ref ss 28(14), 29(9)
GIVEN notice IS A DATE, `other period set by the Board` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`repair costs must be paid by, notice` notice `, other date set` `other period set by the Board` MEANS
    CONSIDER `other period set by the Board`
    WHEN JUST d  THEN d
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `add months` notice 1

§§ `Provisions carried as text`

@ref ss 49, 50(2)-(9), 51, 53, 54, 57, 60, 61, 64-67, 71, 73, 74, 87-91, 93, 94
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`flat provisions carried as text` MEANS
    LIST "s 49: the Board may sell developed land with the Minister's approval; no assurance of sold land is registered without its consent"
         "s 50(2)-(9): a barred purchase may not be presented for registration; the Board gives notice, then vests the title or terminates, and may forfeit moneys paid"
         "s 51: the Board may vary the terms of an application and cancel it, refunding deposit and fees, without liability"
         "ss 53, 54: the Board may execute instruments for a purchaser who fails to, and may act for a party without a solicitor"
         "ss 60, 61: management corporations for Board buildings; the Board or a company may act as one"
         "ss 64, 65: warrants to search and powers to investigate grounds of acquisition"
         "ss 66, 67: vesting of acquired flats and payment or deposit of the compensation the Board determines"
         "s 71: the Minister's direction that property is or is not commercial property is conclusive"
         "s 73: money paid after a notice to quit, acquire or re-enter does not waive it"
         "s 74: rules on sale terms, consents, eligibility, payment, management corporations, use, fees and financial penalties"
         "ss 87-91, 93, 94: the Design-Build-and-Sell Scheme — approved developers, vesting in the Board, Part 4 applied, death of a purchaser before completion"
